# Project Otto — Core

Custom 8-bit TTL homebrew CPU (6502-inspired, not identical). Full reference: `AGENTS.md`.

## Build (always activate venv first)

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
./generate-all.sh              # release — run after ANY kernel or P-Machine change
./generate-all.sh --debug      # debug — includes boot tests
./scripts/build-apps.sh --pascal       # apps only (no ROM rebuild)
./scripts/build-apps.sh --abi v1.2.101 # apps for older kernel EEPROM (Otto hardware)
```

**App commit for Otto hardware (v1.2.101):** after editing `apps/*.asm`, always run
`./scripts/build-apps.sh --abi v1.2.101 <app.asm>` and commit **source +**
`roms/apps/v1.2.101/asm/*.bin` + `catalog.json` together before push. See
`.cursor/rules/otto-assembly.mdc`.
customasm apps/myapp.asm -f binary -o roms/apps/current/asm/myapp.bin
python pascal_compiler.py pascal/examples/hello.pas -o roms/apps/current/pascal/hello.bin
```

Build implementation: `scripts/` (see `scripts/README.md`). Kernel ABI: `kernel/abi/README.md`.

**CustomASM gotcha**: `#include` inside `#if` scopes labels to that block. Put `#if` guards **inside** included files; never wrap `#include` with `#if`.

Unified ROM (kernel + P-Machine) shares 0x0000–0x5FFF. `kernel/build_config.asm` is set by `generate-all.sh`.

## Memory map (essentials)

| Region | Range | Notes |
|--------|-------|-------|
| ROM | 0x0000–0x5FFF | Kernel + P-Machine |
| I/O | 0x6000–0x67FF | Keyboard 0x6000, ACIA 0x6020/0x6021 |
| App RAM | 0x8400–0xEFFF | Apps load here (27 KB) |
| Stack | 0xF000–0xFFFF | Grows down from 0xFFFF |
| Expansion | 0x010000+, 0x020000+ | IDE @ 0x020000, editor source @ 0x010000 |

## Not 6502 — critical differences

1. Branches use **absolute** targets, not relative offsets
2. "Zero page" = 16-bit addr; "absolute" = 24-bit addr
3. Extra registers **D**, **E**; **D:E** is a 16-bit pointer (`LDA DE,X`, `LDA YDE,X`)
4. Overflow flag ≠ 6502 (internal indexing; equals carry)
5. `JSR` is always 4 bytes (opcode + 3-byte address)
6. `INW`/`DEW` for 16-bit memory inc/dec; `SBX` subtracts E from X

## Registers

A, X, Y, D, E (8-bit); OUT (display); PC (24-bit); SP (16-bit, init 0xFFFF).

Flags: N (bit 7), Z, C. Use `CLC` before `ADC`, `SEC` before `SBC`.
